    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">Clean data first, models second. <span>Process models, analysis, and AI are only as good as the record under them. This one is structured before anyone asks.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-runs">
      <li><h3>Attributes ready-made per equipment type</h3><p>Tank orientation to maximum allowed working pressure. You add, remove, or customize; you don't design the schema first.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Relationships on the record</h3><p>Parent and child links for the hierarchy, associations for the rest. You don't rebuild them in a spreadsheet for every study.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Readings with their context</h3><p>Unit, time zone, quality flag, and the original value under any override. You don't clean the same history twice.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Lineage kept</h3><p>Each calculated figure keeps the readings, method, and factor version behind it.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

