<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2>What operations and finance ask about the record.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Which depreciation terms does a record hold?</summary>
        <div><p>Method, in-service date, purchase price, salvage value, useful life, depreciation factor, convention, and dollar rounding. The schedule shows book value, expense, and accumulated depreciation by year.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where does runtime come from?</summary>
        <div><p>A runtime tag on the asset, in hours a month, pulled from SCADA or another field data system, imported, or entered by hand.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which standards is the data model aligned to?</summary>
        <div><p>ISO 55000 for asset management and ISO 14224 for maintenance and reliability data, among others. Aligned to, not certified against.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does the AI read?</summary>
        <div><p>Anomaly detection reads the readings of the tags you pick and compares each with its recent neighbors. The assistant reads your records and shows its sources.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

